  "releaseNotes": "10.1 - conditional steps are a navigation concern now, not a visibility one: a step is\n\t\t\tstepped over rather than removed, so it keeps its index and the wizard keeps its length.\n\t\t\tBREAKING. IsStepVisible -> IsSkipped, and this is a NEGATION, not a rename:\n\t\t\tIsStepVisible=\"False\" becomes IsSkipped=\"True\". StepVisibilityEvaluating,\n\t\t\tStepVisibilityEventArgs and RefreshStepVisibility() are removed - bind IsSkipped, which\n\t\t\tis safe to bind because nothing moves in the visual tree. Also silent: CurrentStepIndex\n\t\t\tand WizardStepInfo.Index now index Steps in full, skipped steps included, where they used\n\t\t\tto index the active flow. See the README for the migration table.",
